# SurgeWhy Cursor Agent Rules (Open Agent Hackathon 2026 - Track 2)

Always read `AGENTS.md` before changing any Data, Build, or Power code.

## 1. Track 2 Explainability Contract
- Every verdict must output: (a) a cited Causal Proof Chain (`[schema.table#id]`), (b) a Ruled-Out Hypotheses Ledger, (c) quantitative Counterfactual Flip Deltas, and (d) a calibrated confidence score that triggers `NEEDS_EVIDENCE` below `0.75`.
- Never use em-dashes in UI copy, prompts, markdown docs, or slide decks; use hyphens or colons.

## 2. Layer 01 (DATA - Zetaris)
- Run `python3 scripts/preflight.py` before modifying Zetaris schemas.
- Send strictly **one SQL statement per REST call** to `POST {ZETARIS_REST_URL}/sql-editor/sqls/run` with `Authorization: Bearer`, `X-Org-ID: 1`, and a fresh UUID4 `X-Request-ID`.
- Never print secrets from `.env`.

## 3. Layer 02 (BUILD - Cursor & Meterless Engines)
- Keep all four Meterless Engines (`scout_intent.py`, `world_model.py`, `markovian.py`, `h_mem.py`) active in the adjudication loop and covered by `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v`.
- Keep `metadata.json` and `README.md` synced with Cursor and Meterless Engine usage.

## 4. Layer 03 (POWER - Meterless Nightshift & NVIDIA Nemotron)
- Route all model calls through Meterless Nightshift (`http://127.0.0.1:8088/v1`) with `meterless-app: surgewhy-agent` and `meterless-scope: user`.
- Pin `nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b` (Lane 1 Fast) and `nvidia/nemotron-3.5-super-vl-120b-a12b` (Lane 2 Deep) and log a `ModelReceipt` on every step.
